@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy</PageTitle>

<div class="settings-shell">
    <section class="card-surface settings-card">
        <p class="section-label">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Data handling</h1>
        <p class="panel-copy">
            Personal sync keeps Habitica API tokens in this browser. Shared party sync sends credentials to the Cloudflare Pages Function only to verify current party membership with Habitica.
        </p>

        <div class="settings-grid">
            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Cloudflare Pages migration note</h2>
                <p>If you opened the Pages deployment before the service-worker rollback, unregister the old service worker, clear site data, and hard refresh once so cached redirected responses are removed.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Habitica credentials</h2>
                <p>Credentials are used to call Habitica from the browser and to derive encrypted personal sync keys. They are not included in exports. The shared party sync endpoint receives credentials only for membership verification before reading or writing party CRON data.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Local and exported data</h2>
                <p>Snapshots, party history, diagnostics, gear catalog data, and equipment presets are stored in browser storage. Exported backup files are not encrypted.</p>
            </MudPaper>

            <MudPaper Class="card-surface action-card" Elevation="0">
                <h2>Cloudflare sync</h2>
                <p>Personal Cloudflare sync stores encrypted KV blobs. Shared party sync stores party CRON history and derived party state in D1 after membership verification. Cloudflare may process request metadata such as IP address and timestamps as part of hosting and security operations.</p>
            </MudPaper>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
